WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.710
A physicist can describe a whole theory

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.421
of gravity in one line of LaTeX.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.470
Getting the field equations back out of

4
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.564
a computer algebra system can take weeks.

5
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.530
Project Noether is built to close

6
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:13.990
that gap.

7
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.010
It is a symbolic physics collaborator,

8
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.100
about forty three thousand lines

9
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:19.560
of Python.

10
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.880
The hard part here is not

11
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:22.829
the mathematics.

12
00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:26.430
Kernels like Cadabra, xAct, and SymPy are

13
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.078
already rigorous and powerful.

14
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.620
Using them means hand translating notation

15
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.861
and declaring every symmetry yourself.

16
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.500
Then you read the answer back out

17
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.467
of a machine dialect.

18
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.670
Noether takes over that translation layer,

19
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.503
and leaves the algebra to the kernels.

20
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:44.940
The tool runs a four beat loop,

21
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.405
the way a careful collaborator would.

22
00:00:47.705 --> 00:00:50.500
First, you state the action in LaTeX.

23
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.070
Next, Noether interrogates you, and you

24
00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.109
answer the questions that matter.

25
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.320
Then the kernels compute, and a

26
00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.548
verification layer checks the result.

27
00:00:59.848 --> 00:01:02.700
Underneath, this is a state machine that

28
00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:04.670
runs from ingest all the way

29
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.130
to present.

30
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.929
Four layers sit behind that loop.

31
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.940
Thin frontends, a Python orchestrator,

32
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.455
kernel adapters, and a verification layer.

33
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.401
Two hard boundaries cut across them.

34
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.040
The key point is that each boundary

35
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.501
enforces exactly one product promise.

36
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.550
They are enforced mechanically, in code,

37
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.046
not by reviewer discipline.

38
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.600
The first boundary is the Noether Problem

39
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.097
Representation, the NPR.

40
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.110
It is a versioned pydantic schema holding

41
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.560
geometry, objects, the action, and

42
00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:37.020
the task.

43
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.150
It is the only language the orchestrator

44
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:40.999
speaks to a kernel.

45
00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:44.200
Kernels never see raw user LaTeX, and

46
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.205
results never carry kernel syntax.

47
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.860
That is what keeps the system from

48
00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.815
marrying a single algebra backend.

49
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.910
The second promise is that the tool

50
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:54.586
never guesses.

51
00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.820
Every open question lands in an ambiguity

52
00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.686
ledger attached to the problem.

53
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.400
While that ledger is not empty, the

54
00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.317
planner simply refuses to plan.

55
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.020
The model may propose answers, and it

56
00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:08.713
always shows its reasoning.

57
00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.630
But only a confirmed human answer can

58
00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.789
change the problem.

59
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.670
An off menu answer is rejected, and

60
00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.462
the session is left untouched.

61
00:02:18.012 --> 00:02:20.980
Physics conventions are never implied in

62
00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:21.596
this codebase.

63
00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.590
Signature, curvature sign, torsion sign,

64
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.600
and ten more fields travel with

65
00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.592
every expression.

66
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.590
Under an independent connection, some of

67
00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.110
those stop being defaults and

68
00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:32.991
become questions.

69
00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.880
The Ricci contraction is one, because

70
00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.963
Ricci is no longer symmetric there.

71
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.350
Change one field and the answer changes,

72
00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.020
so nothing is assumed silently.

73
00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.084
Here is a single derivation, end

74
00:02:46.094 --> 00:02:46.706
to end.

75
00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.810
The orchestrator asks the model to write

76
00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:50.675
a kernel script.

77
00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.877
That script carries no authority at all.

78
00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.800
It runs sandboxed, and the kernel checks

79
00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.635
its own residue inside the script.

80
00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.380
Only that check can set the

81
00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.050
verified flag.

82
00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.680
Remember it this way: the model

83
00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.531
orchestrates, and the kernel decides.

84
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.663
Two kernels do the computing today.

85
00:03:09.963 --> 00:03:13.070
Cadabra 2 runs as a sandboxed subprocess,

86
00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.211
driving frozen audited scripts.

87
00:03:15.511 --> 00:03:18.280
SymPy runs in process as an independent

88
00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:20.375
oracle on explicit backgrounds.

89
00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.190
The planner chooses between them by

90
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.792
capability, never by name.

91
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.450
There is also a compute path that

92
00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.783
needs no model at all.

93
00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.480
When an action decomposes into known

94
00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:34.190
building blocks, the kernel assembles and

95
00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:34.650
checks it.

96
00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:37.290
Every answer climbs a five rung

97
00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.657
verification ladder.

98
00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.510
It starts at well formedness and ends

99
00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.330
at independent recomputation.

100
00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.320
For metric affine geometry, two kernels

101
00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.190
must agree before anything is

102
00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.070
called verified.

103
00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.740
That dual gate exists to catch one

104
00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.231
specific failure mode.

105
00:03:53.531 --> 00:03:56.300
A Levi Civita shortcut can silently drop

106
00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.410
a torsion term and still report a

107
00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.291
zero residue.

108
00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.080
The repository calls that the

109
00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:02.685
torsion trap.

110
00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.050
When Noether cannot finish a calculation,

111
00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.096
it says so plainly.

112
00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.350
The higher Horndeski densities need

113
00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.540
derivative ordering machinery that is not

114
00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:12.943
installed here.

115
00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.050
Those requests come back unverified, with

116
00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.171
a detail line naming the blocker.

117
00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.380
A gated result is always distinguishable

118
00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.631
from a confirmed one.

119
00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.860
A fabricated answer would be far worse

120
00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:26.963
than an honest not yet.

121
00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.860
Four frontends share that single

122
00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:30.862
session surface.

123
00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.080
A command line loop, an HTTP API,

124
00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.538
an MCP server, and a web client.

125
00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.790
None of them run physics, in the

126
00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.443
browser or in the terminal.

127
00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:43.460
A host model calling the MCP tools

128
00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.906
gets refusals as ordinary data.

129
00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.640
So it cannot pressure Noether into

130
00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:49.619
guessing on its behalf.

131
00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.910
Every run writes a provenance bundle

132
00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:53.370
to disk.

133
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.760
The kernel script, the raw output, the

134
00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.710
assumptions snapshot, and every

135
00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:58.320
check verdict.

136
00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:01.250
That history reloads identically across

137
00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.960
the server, the tools, and the

138
00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:03.484
web client.

139
00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.440
If a later answer changes an assumption,

140
00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.392
earlier results are marked stale.

141
00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.530
They are never quietly trusted, and never

142
00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.404
silently dropped.

143
00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.250
The churn history tells you where to

144
00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.069
start reading.

145
00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.862
The derive path and the Cadabra templates

146
00:05:18.872 --> 00:05:20.422
absorbed the most change.

147
00:05:20.722 --> 00:05:23.020
Eighty three test and eval files hold

148
00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.626
the contract in place.

149
00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.360
So remember three things about

150
00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.297
this repository.

151
00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.880
Kernels compute, the model only

152
00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.500
orchestrates, and ambiguity always comes

153
00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:33.960
back to you.

154
00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.790
That boundary is the whole product.
